  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Let \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) be two-digit positive integers with mean \\(60.\\) What is the maximum value of the ratio \\(\\dfrac{x}{y}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{33}{7}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{39}{7}\\)",
    "D": "\\(9\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{99}{10}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The mean gives a fixed sum:\n\\[\nx+y=2\\cdot60=120.\n\\]\nSince \\(x\\) is a two-digit integer, \\(x\\le99\\), so \\(y=120-x\\ge21\\). Both numbers are positive, and therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{y}\\le\\frac{99}{y}\\le\\frac{99}{21}=\\frac{33}{7}.\n\\]\nThe pair \\((x,y)=(99,21)\\) consists of two-digit positive integers and has mean \\(60\\), so it attains the bound. The maximum is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{33}{7}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
